
  <sn><md>### Set Operations {.text-center}

:::.row
:::.col-12 .col-lg-7
### Union of Sets

* **Definition:** The set formed by `combining all the elements of two or more sets` is called a union set.
* **Notation:** Expressed as $A \cup B$ and read as *"A union B"*.
* **Set Builder Form:** $A \cup B = \{x : x \in A \text{ or } x \in B\}$.
:::

:::.col-12 .col-lg-5
![img](https://www.mathstopia.net/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/union-two-sets.jpg)
:::
:::


**Example 7:** If $C = \{\text{Razzaq, Sakip, Alok}\}$ and $D = \{\text{Alok, Mushfiq}\}$, 
then $C \cup D = \{\text{Razzaq, Sakip, Alok, Mushfiq}\}$.

**Example 8:** If $R = \{x : x \text{ is factor of } 6\} = \{1, 2, 3, 6\}$ and $S = \{x : x \text{ is factor of } 8\} = \{1, 2, 4, 8\}$, 
then $R \cup S = \{1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8\}$.

</md></sn>
